WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:20.356
The next morning The Lemonade Detectives discussed the mystery as they put the finishing touches on their float.

2
00:00:20.357 --> 00:00:25.414
"Let's list everything suspicious that's happened," Henry suggested.

3
00:00:25.415 --> 00:00:27.329
"Okay," Cole said.

4
00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:32.190
"The first thing we found out about was that threat on the website."

5
00:00:32.191 --> 00:00:37.709
"True," Henry said. "But that wasn't the first thing that happened.

6
00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:40.816
The threat appeared sometime yesterday.

7
00:00:40.817 --> 00:00:45.753
Mrs. Sweet's candy disappeared before that, on Thursday night."

8
00:00:45.754 --> 00:00:48.861
"Don't forget Mr. Fleming's threat," Maggie said.

9
00:00:48.862 --> 00:00:51.283
"That happened yesterday too."

10
00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:57.025
"So did Jackson's comment about the parade being cancelled," Henry finished.

11
00:00:57.026 --> 00:00:59.346
"So who are our suspects?"

12
00:00:59.347 --> 00:01:01.776
"Jackson," Cole said.

13
00:01:01.777 --> 00:01:07.775
"If your theory is right, he could be trying to create an interesting story to write about."

14
00:01:07.776 --> 00:01:12.705
"Yeah," Maggie said. "I think Snake is a better suspect, though."

15
00:01:12.706 --> 00:01:16.647
"Snake?" Henry had forgotten about the teenager.

16
00:01:16.648 --> 00:01:22.291
"Why?" Henry asked Maggie. "His band isn't even making a float anymore."

17
00:01:22.292 --> 00:01:24.459
"Exactly," Maggie said.

18
00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:28.512
"This stuff started happening after the band dropped out of the parade.

19
00:01:28.513 --> 00:01:31.402
Maybe Snake is mad about dropping out.

20
00:01:31.403 --> 00:01:34.986
And now he doesn't want anyone else to win those prizes either."

21
00:01:34.987 --> 00:01:41.593
"Maybe," Henry said. "I guess we should keep him on the list. Who else?"

22
00:01:41.594 --> 00:01:44.004
"Mr. Newman," Cole said.

23
00:01:44.005 --> 00:01:46.832
"What about him?" Maggie asked.

24
00:01:46.833 --> 00:01:52.525
Cole shrugged. "He was in Mrs. Sweet's shed the night her candy disappeared."

25
00:01:52.526 --> 00:01:54.552
"True," Henry said.

26
00:01:54.553 --> 00:02:03.521
"The rumor Jackson started and the threat from Mr. Fleming could be red herrings—false clues that are confusing us.

27
00:02:03.522 --> 00:02:07.297
Why do you think Mr. Newman should be a suspect?"

28
00:02:07.298 --> 00:02:11.128
"You said his daughter is in Snake's band," Cole said.

29
00:02:11.129 --> 00:02:16.390
"Maybe Mr. Newman wanted to sabotage other floats because of that."

30
00:02:16.391 --> 00:02:19.007
"Maybe," Henry said.

31
00:02:19.008 --> 00:02:24.764
"But he didn't seem very excited about the band when I heard him talking to Jade."

32
00:02:24.765 --> 00:02:29.112
"Yeah," Maggie agreed. "But what about Miss Bishop?

33
00:02:29.113 --> 00:02:32.650
She was sneaking around Mrs. Sweet's shed yesterday."

34
00:02:32.651 --> 00:02:37.983
"True," Cole said. "But she has no reason to want the parade cancelled.

35
00:02:37.984 --> 00:02:41.915
So she probably didn't post that threat on the website."

36
00:02:41.916 --> 00:02:44.452
"I guess you're right," Henry agreed.

37
00:02:44.453 --> 00:02:48.454
"That leaves one more suspect: Mr. Fleming."

38
00:02:48.455 --> 00:02:53.287
Maggie nodded. "He definitely wants the parade shut down."

39
00:02:53.288 --> 00:02:58.175
"But why would he steal Mrs. Sweet's candy?" Henry asked.

40
00:02:58.176 --> 00:03:02.027
"Who knows?" Cole grabbed a bottle of glue.

41
00:03:02.028 --> 00:03:05.562
"Let's finish our float and then go try to find out.

42
00:03:05.563 --> 00:03:12.490
We still have a few hours to investigate before the parade starts."

43
00:03:12.491 --> 00:03:19.058
An hour later The Lemonade Detectives waved to Maggie's dad as he drove away down the street on his tractor.

44
00:03:19.059 --> 00:03:21.708
The float was on the cart behind him.

45
00:03:21.709 --> 00:03:26.440
It was covered in a sheet so nobody would see it until the parade started.

46
00:03:26.441 --> 00:03:30.831
"I'll meet you kids at the high school at three o'clock," Maggie's dad said.

47
00:03:30.832 --> 00:03:35.362
"See you then," Henry called back. "Thanks, Uncle Bruce!"

48
00:03:35.363 --> 00:03:40.836
Henry and his friends walked to Mr. Fleming's house.

49
00:03:40.837 --> 00:03:45.454
A plump older woman was out in the yard watering some flowers.

50
00:03:45.455 --> 00:03:49.055
"That's his wife," Cole whispered to the others.

51
00:03:49.056 --> 00:03:53.067
Then he waved to the woman. "Hi, Mrs. Fleming!"

52
00:03:53.068 --> 00:03:59.001
"Oh, hello, Cole!" Mrs. Fleming put down her watering can and hurried over.

53
00:03:59.002 --> 00:04:04.776
"It's so nice to see you! Are you excited for the parade this afternoon?"

54
00:04:04.777 --> 00:04:07.312
"Definitely," Cole said.

55
00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:12.662
"We heard your husband isn't very happy about the parade," Henry put in.

56
00:04:12.663 --> 00:04:16.830
"He thinks everyone is being too noisy building their floats."

57
00:04:16.831 --> 00:04:22.416
Mrs. Fleming sighed. "Yes, I know. He's been complaining all week.

58
00:04:22.417 --> 00:04:24.822
He hates noise.

59
00:04:24.823 --> 00:04:30.706
He's always yelling at the neighbors about their barking dogs or their loud lawn mowers."

60
00:04:30.707 --> 00:04:35.124
She smiled at the kids. "He's really a nice man, though.

61
00:04:35.125 --> 00:04:38.615
Too much noise just makes him cranky."

62
00:04:38.616 --> 00:04:40.664
Maggie stepped forward.

63
00:04:40.665 --> 00:04:46.797
"Do you think he was crabby enough to post a threatening message on the town website?" she asked.

64
00:04:46.798 --> 00:04:51.572
Mrs. Fleming chuckled. "Oh my, no," she said.

65
00:04:51.573 --> 00:04:57.219
"My husband hates computers. He won't touch one unless he has to.

66
00:04:57.220 --> 00:05:01.645
He even asks me to send emails to his clients for him."

67
00:05:01.646 --> 00:05:07.247
"Yes, that's true," Henry said. "Sorry to bother you, Mrs. Fleming."

68
00:05:07.248 --> 00:05:11.973
"It's no bother at all." Mrs. Fleming waved as they walked away.

69
00:05:11.974 --> 00:05:14.657
"Enjoy the parade, kids!"

70
00:05:14.658 --> 00:05:20.823
"She's a lot nicer than her husband," Maggie said as The Lemonade Detectives headed down the sidewalk.

71
00:05:20.824 --> 00:05:26.335
"Yeah," Henry said. "It sounds like Mr. Fleming isn't the culprit.

72
00:05:26.336 --> 00:05:31.438
He hates computers, so he probably wouldn't have posted that threat."

73
00:05:31.439 --> 00:05:37.600
Cole nodded. "Plus, it's hard to imagine him breaking into Mrs. Sweet's shed.

74
00:05:37.601 --> 00:05:40.261
So who should we investigate next?"

75
00:05:40.262 --> 00:05:43.448
"How about Jackson?" Henry suggested.

76
00:05:43.449 --> 00:05:51.820
"Let's go to the newspaper office and see if he's there."

77
00:05:51.821 --> 00:05:54.368
Soon they reached the office.

78
00:05:54.369 --> 00:05:59.909
"I'm sorry, kids," the receptionist told them. "Jackson isn't here.

79
00:05:59.910 --> 00:06:01.677
He just rushed out.

80
00:06:01.678 --> 00:06:10.951
He said there's some urgent breaking news that will make the newspaper's front page!"
